u,j}(M)\le C_h L+C_h n_e-c_h d_e-2\pi jv +C_h(v^2+(1+f)|v|). \end{equation} \item Assume the common hypotheses of parts 3 and 4 of Proposition ef{prop:03-trial-bounds}, polynomial bounds on \(n_e,|j|,|M|,\ell_e\), and \(
u_\sigma\asymp m\). Choose the imaginary imbalance and trial density from part 3 of that proposition. Then  egin{equation} \mathcal L_{
u,j}(M)\le C_h L+C_h n_e-c_h d_e-c_\delta U^2 L+o(L). \end{equation} If \(U\le U_0\), the choice from part 4 instead gives  egin{equation} \mathcal L_{
u,j}(M)\le rac{3\gamma L}{8} -2L rac{\operatorname{Re}(\eta^2)}{4\kappa} +C\varepsilon L+o(L)+C_h n_e-c_{h,\varepsilon}d_e. \end{equation} Here \(\delta\) can be taken sufficiently small without degrading the displayed damping and per-particle constants, and \(U_0\) may then be fixed arbitrarily, as in part 4 of that proposition. \end{enumerate} The estimates are uniform once the parameters in the trial bounds and the polynomial size powers are fixed.
